74
00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.850
he played to vinyl to LP, the records

75
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.390
and brought music in the house.

76
00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:56.260
And then his friends happened to be incredible musicians.

77
00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.220
And we lived growing up in the Bay Area

78
00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:00.000
in Oakland, San Francisco,

79
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.810
it's just like everyone was from there.

80
00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.300
Carlos Santana, Grateful Dead,

81
00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.110
these people were coming to our house

82
00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.330
and we would be able to jam with them

83
00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.990
and so I watched my dad play,

84
00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:11.090
even though I was training to be in the Olympics.

85
00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.770
I was a track star.

86
00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:16.270 line:15%
